  "output": {
    "answer": "The split wasn't picked after I saw the win — it's the frozen eval split that landed at 19:24 PDT while the head was still fitting, held out by scene, artwork family, and crop file. A separate hold-out check confirmed none of the 201 test crops trained or tuned the head: it fits only on catalogue render rows, tunes its one parameter on a disjoint dev split, and a filename join plus cosine check found no test photo in any training crop. I still didn't treat that same-split lift as proof — it shipped behind a flag, and production only flipped after an independent replay: 12 fixed, none broken.",
